# =====================================================================
# Line endings
#
# Single source of truth for this repository. It wins over whatever
# core.autocrlf a machine happens to have configured locally.
#
# Reason: the CI runner is Linux and checks out LF. Without this file
# Windows keeps CRLF in the working copy, so "npm run format:check"
# would fail locally while passing in CI, which makes the check
# useless.
# =====================================================================

# Default: Git detects text files on its own, always stores them with
# LF, and thanks to eol=lf checks them out with LF on Windows too.
* text=auto eol=lf

# --- Windows tools expect CRLF ---
*.bat   text eol=crlf
*.cmd   text eol=crlf
*.ps1   text eol=crlf

# --- Binary files: Git must never convert these ---
*.png   -text
*.jpg   -text
*.jpeg  -text
*.ico   -text
*.woff2 -text
